    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n97 Salthill is an exceptional two-bedroom apartment, formerly configured as a three-bedroom, ideally positioned on the second floor within this prestigious gated development. Beautifully refurbished and presented in excellent condition throughout, the apartment benefits from an enviable triple aspect, with three separate balconies and spectacular sea views. The combination of its elevated position and extensive glazing ensures the property enjoys an abundance of natural light.\n\nThe well-proportioned accommodation extends to approximately 100 sq. m (1,076 sq. ft) with a further 39 sq.m. (420 sq.ft.) of external space. The apartment has been comprehensively refurbished to create a beautifully appointed interior. The superb kitchen/dining room incorporates an extensive range of fitted cabinetry together with a large central island, while direct access is provided to two adjoining balconies, including a particularly spacious south-facing terrace, ideal for outdoor dining and relaxation.\n\nThe separate living room is particularly impressive, generously proportioned and centred around an attractive open fireplace with bespoke fitted cabinetry and shelving. Glazed doors frame magnificent views across Dublin Bay and open directly onto a further balcony, from which the superb sea views can be fully enjoyed. The triple-aspect arrangement is a defining feature of the apartment, with balconies positioned to the front, rear and side providing a variety of outlooks over the sea, surrounding coastline and beautifully maintained landscaped grounds.\n\nThe bedroom accommodation is equally well considered. The main bedroom is a generous double room with an extensive range of fitted wardrobes and storage, together with direct access to one of the balconies and an en suite bathroom. A second double bedroom, also with fitted storage, and a separate bathroom complete the accommodation. Lift access within the building and surface parking further enhance the convenience of this apartment.\n\nConstructed circa 1991 by the renowned Cosgrave developers in the grounds of the former Salthill Hotel, Salthill is one of Monkstown's most highly regarded residential developments. Apartments in Block D of the development are the most sought after and rarely come to the market. They are famous for providing generously proportioned accommodation with stunning views in a secure environment within walking distance of the excellent amenities within Monkstown Village and excellent transport.\n\nSalthill/Monkstown DART station is immediately adjacent, while the villages of Monkstown and Dun Laoghaire are within easy walking distance, offering an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, shops and everyday amenities. The seafront and Dun Laoghaire Harbour are also close at hand, with a marina, four yacht clubs, coastal walks and extensive recreational facilities."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nReception Hall - 1.8m x 3m\nwith built in storage and cabinetry, ceiling coving, oak timber flooring, recessed lighting and glazed double doors leading to\n\nDining Area - 3.9m x 6.7m\nwith oak timber flooring, built in cabinetry with gas fired boiler, door to terrace to the front and door to side balcony\n\nKitchen - \nhand painted kitchen with a range of press and drawer units, large centre island, four ring ceramic hob with extractor over, double ovens, integrated dishwasher, american style fridge/freezer, silestone worktops and splashback, circular porthole window looking over the bay, door to hotpress and open arch leading to\n\nLiving Room - 5.6m x 4.7m\nwide plank oak timber flooring, stone fireplace with stone hearth and gas coal effect fire, built in cabinetry and shelving, ceiling coving and double doors leading to balcony overlooking Dublin bay and further door leading to the side balcony\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.7m x 3.4m\nwith oak timber flooring, built in fitted wardrobes, picture window overlooking the bay, door to the balcony and door to\n\nEnsuite - \ncomprising cabinet wash hand basin, w.c., corner shower, heated towel rail, tiled floor and tiled walls\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.4m x 3.1m\nwith oak timber flooring, floor to ceiling built in fitted wardrobes and door to terrace.\n\nBathroom - \ncomprising cabinet wash hand basin, w.c., corner shower, heated towel rail, tiled floor and tiled walls\n\nTerrace - 7.1m x 3.1m\nwith magnificent views over the communal grounds.\n\nSide balcony - 6m x 1.3m\nwith stunning views over Dublin bay and beyond.\n\nRear Balcony - 2m x 4.6m\nwith panoramic views over the bay.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Stunning sea views across Dublin Bay</li><li>Exceptional second-floor two-bedroom apartment</li><li>Accommodation extending to 100 sq.m. (1,076 sq. ft) with a further 3 balconies comprising 39 sq.m. (420 sq.ft.) </li><li>Beautifully refurbished and presented in excellent condition throughout</li><li>Spectacular evening sunsets from the balcony</li><li>Rare triple-aspect orientation with an abundance of natural light</li><li>Three separate balconies to the front, rear and side</li><li>Gas fired central heating</li><li>Open-plan kitchen/dining room with large central island</li><li>Generously proportioned separate living room with open fireplace</li><li>Lift access</li><li>Surface and underground parking</li><li>Secure gated development with beautifully maintained landscaped grounds</li><li>Immediately adjacent to Salthill/Monkstown DART station</li><li>Within a short stroll of Monkstown village, Dun Laoghaire, the seafront and harbour</ul>"
      },
